      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T00:03:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@waihong@google.com I wanted to see if changing this would cause any problems for any tools that you know about.\n\nOn the fingerprint side, we have a bunch of scripts that parse the version string based on the format that was used for the EC version. Instead of changing all of those, I wanted to see if it would cause problems to just change the Zephyr version string.\n\n(Right now this is just a proposal to get feedback from anyone who might be affected, so feel free to add anyone else relevant.)",
      "revId": "8deff2193a853650d2a5b29241f5b914b4072a97",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f752225c_8c562166",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T18:21:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are multiple formats of the EC versions. They all should be supported, as they are placed in the RO.\n\nFor example:\n cros ec: pompom_v2.0.26430+6e46d6606f\n old zephyr: frostflow_v3.3.107034-ec:c77a44\n new zephyr: rex-16097.0.0-6e46d66+\n\nChanging \u0027-\u0027 to \u0027_\u0027 doesn\u0027t make it compatible with the cros ec format. It introduces a new format and we need to modify multiple places to support anther format.",
      "parentUuid": "8a37c850_afc33529",
      "revId": "8deff2193a853650d2a5b29241f5b914b4072a97",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b081a2a2_72a87566",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T22:16:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Changing \u0027-\u0027 to \u0027_\u0027 doesn\u0027t make it compatible with the cros ec format.\n\nIt depends on what part of the string you care about. It does make the format consistent for pulling out the board name, since it would always be `board_\u003csome other string\u003e`. On the fingerprint side that\u0027s pretty much all we do when parsing the version since the version string is just considered a \"blob\".\n\nHave you already shipped Zephyr devices with RO versions that are `board-\u003csome string\u003e`? If so, then I guess it\u0027s too late to change.",
      "parentUuid": "f752225c_8c562166",
      "revId": "8deff2193a853650d2a5b29241f5b914b4072a97",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "458cc145_aef6de78",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T22:25:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Multiple devices have been shipped with the new zephyr format, like karis, screebo. It is too late.\n\nSince some EC board names contain \u0027_\u0027, not so simple that we use regex to match some non-trivial pattern.",
      "parentUuid": "b081a2a2_72a87566",
      "revId": "8deff2193a853650d2a5b29241f5b914b4072a97",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
